-- tests-independent.l4
-- Independent test author's file for the Interpretation Act (Canada) encoding.
-- Every expected value comes from ANSWERS.md, which was written from the source text before any .l4 file was opened.
-- One #ASSERT per scenario, numbered #N as in ANSWERS.md.  A scenario with no function to ask is listed as a GAP line.
-- An assertion that fails is a finding and is left failing.  "dup of #N" means the encoding answers this scenario and #N with one and the same call.
-- Where my text says "no" and the encoding refuses (its convention is REFUSE), the assertion is written with the answer I expect, and a refusal then shows as "assertion refused".

-- Test inputs of mine (not the encoding's): the "other holidays" of s.35(1) that the text names but does not date,
-- supplied by the caller as the time module expects (flagged EXT in ANSWERS.md).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`named days that the text does not date` d MEANS
        (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1)
     OR (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 7 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1)
     OR (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 11 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 11)
     OR (DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY d EQUALS 25)
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2024 3 29
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2024 4 1
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2024 5 20
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2025 4 18
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2025 4 21
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2025 5 19
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 3
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 4 6
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2026 5 18
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2027 3 26
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2027 3 29
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2027 5 24
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2028 4 14
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2028 4 17
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2028 5 22
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2029 3 30
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2029 4 2
     OR d EQUALS YMD 2029 5 21

-- the full s.35(1) holiday test for scenarios that need Sunday, Labour Day and September 30 as well
`my holidays` MEANS `the holiday test of section 35(1), given the other holidays` `named days that the text does not date`

-- the s.26 roll, under my holidays
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`my last day when the time ends on` d MEANS
    `the last day on which a thing may be done when the time limited ends on` d `given the holidays` `my holidays`

-- Commencement facts that I construct for the scenarios
`facts of an Act, assented 2024-06-20, naming no day` MEANS
    `Commencement facts of an Act`
        WITH `the day the Act was assented to` IS YMD 2024 6 20
             `what the provision says about when it comes into force` IS `it names no day`

`facts of an Act, assented 2024-06-20, provision naming 2025-01-01` MEANS
    `Commencement facts of an Act`
        WITH `the day the Act was assented to` IS YMD 2024 6 20
             `what the provision says about when it comes into force` IS `it names a particular day` (YMD 2025 1 1)

`facts of a regulation made 2024-03-10, naming no day, registered 2024-03-15, not exempt` MEANS
    `Commencement facts of a regulation`
        WITH `the day the regulation was made` IS YMD 2024 3 10
             `what the regulation says about when it comes into force` IS `it names no day`
             `the day it was registered under section 6 of the Statutory Instruments Act, if it has been` IS JUST (YMD 2024 3 15)
             `it is of a class exempted from the application of subsection 5(1) of that Act` IS FALSE

`facts of a regulation made 2024-03-10, naming no day, registered 2024-03-15, exempted class` MEANS
    `Commencement facts of a regulation`
        WITH `the day the regulation was made` IS YMD 2024 3 10
             `what the regulation says about when it comes into force` IS `it names no day`
             `the day it was registered under section 6 of the Statutory Instruments Act, if it has been` IS JUST (YMD 2024 3 15)
             `it is of a class exempted from the application of subsection 5(1) of that Act` IS TRUE

`facts of a regulation naming 2024-09-01` MEANS
    `Commencement facts of a regulation`
        WITH `the day the regulation was made` IS YMD 2024 3 10
             `what the regulation says about when it comes into force` IS `it names a particular day` (YMD 2024 9 1)
             `the day it was registered under section 6 of the Statutory Instruments Act, if it has been` IS NOTHING
             `it is of a class exempted from the application of subsection 5(1) of that Act` IS FALSE

-- Days Parliament sits, for the s.39(1) scenarios (mine): weekdays from 2025-09-15 on.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my sitting days` d MEANS
        d AT LEAST YMD 2025 9 15
    AND NOT (`Weekday of` d EQUALS Saturday)
    AND NOT (`Weekday of` d EQUALS Sunday)

-- Days Parliament sits, daily (for the "then sitting" limb)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my daily sitting` d MEANS TRUE

