-- ===== Enacting Clause (s.4) =====
#ASSERT `the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form` "Her Majesty, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate and House of Commons of Canada, enacts as follows:"   -- #38 s.4(1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the enacting clause of an Act may be in the form` "Be it enacted by the Parliament of Canada as follows:"   -- #39 s.4(1) (NC)
#ASSERT `an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` TRUE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE   -- #40 s.4(2)
#ASSERT NOT `an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` FALSE `and the provisions follow the clause` TRUE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE   -- #41 s.4(2) clause before preamble
#ASSERT NOT `an Act is arranged as section 4(2) requires where` TRUE `and the enacting clause follows it` TRUE `and the provisions follow the clause` FALSE `and are concise and enunciative` TRUE   -- #42 s.4(2) body must follow clause

