-- ===== Property and Civil Rights (s.8.1, s.8.2), Indigenous Peoples (s.8.3) =====
#ASSERT `is an equally authoritative and recognized source of the law of property and civil rights in Canada` `the common law` AND `is an equally authoritative and recognized source of the law of property and civil rights in Canada` `the civil law`   -- #101 s.8.1
#ASSERT `the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` FALSE EQUALS `those in force in the province at the time the enactment is being applied`   -- #102 s.8.1 time of application
-- RECONCILED #103: reviewer wrote `#ASSERT NOT (`the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` TRUE EQUALS `those in force in the province at the time the enactment is b`; triaged against the text: the function returns a value (a day, a class, a name or a rule) and the Act gives none for this case, so the encoding refuses; the reviewer's NOT (f ... EQUALS v) was the wrong shape for a case the Act does not answer (reviewer's triage, label SHAPE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the province's rules, principles and concepts to which reference is made, unless` TRUE   -- #103 s.8.1 otherwise provided by law
